> "Haakon Studebaker" <heptapod@yahoo.com> wrote

> > Why not make it possible to put sacks on your head to induce blindness?

> perhaps you'd suffocate if you put a bag over your head?  It seems that
> there are plenty of ways to induce blindness, why have another item that has
> dual purposes and thus makes blindfolds less than useful?

You'd probably have to require that the sack be empty. Sacks of all
stripes weigh more than blindfolds or towels, so a sack would probably
not be a long-term solution. To make them more useful, you might
include a way to put sacks on other creatures' heads, blinding them.
(As noted, foocubi might us this on a hero with very low charisma. In
that case, the foocubi's result is likely to be bad enough - I'd
suggest such sacks be uncursed.)

Hmm, here's a thought. Require that the sack be both empty and
_wielded_. From there, you could [P]ut it on, or attack with it. This
shouldn't violate pacifist conduct. That would make it a big pain in
the ass to use to facilitate telepathy, give pacifists another silly
trick, and add a bit of flavor.

